  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "S2 keeps the 5% limit but allows up to 60 months to comply and does not stop sales of models between 5% and 8%, with 8% as the new-marketing bar; existing models are not exempt, and customers receive numerical per-model rates while the public does not. S5 imposes a mandatory recall at 8 per 100,000 with no transition period, which bites on Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9. S3 allows a 6-year retrofit for installed units, which favours Northwind's 38% shut-off coverage."
